values ('e5f6a7b8-9c0d-4f44-9b34-4c5d6e7f8a44', 'world-literature', 'World Literature', 'Students study what world literature means, how texts circulate, and how comparison can be rigorous rather than superficial, treating translation as method, mediation, power, language texture, and interpretive problem. The sequence moves from ancient, sacred, medieval, and early modern literatures through Enlightenment and Romantic exchange, the global novel, modernism, postcolonial critique, diaspora, and intersectional reading. Later work covers contemporary publishing and canon formation, climate and speculative futures, digital circulation, and a comparative research project.');

