iction, and hybrid forms."}, {"id": "5818dcc4-ea8d-4dbf-8a34-922b3032d933", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Publishing and prizes", "children": [{"id": "619e4257-1392-4ea2-9951-57e1d5f06a5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Booker"}, {"id": "b0f8e94a-2568-4374-9ed9-a860a10346f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Nobel"}, {"id": "378772a0-1dee-426a-8225-147a7c26d41f", "type": "concept", "title": "International Booker"}, {"id": "782181a1-96cf-4d51-a6a1-65416679484f", "type": "concept", "title": "Caine Prize"}, {"id": "69c32530-90e9-49e3-88ce-52bc2a41b8b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Neustadt Prize"}, {"id": "98352dd8-2e59-4077-a197-3bf7b0357044", "type": "concept", "title": "small presses"}, {"id": "9cea29be-7a5f-49a9-a762-cb3b1d31b14f", "type": "concept", "title": "rights sales"}, {"id": "f8d5ed68-d52d-4e6e-b87c-f0860ceb8c10", "type": "concept", "title": "translation grants"}], "description": "World-literary value is produced through institutions, not discovered in a vacuum."}, {"id": "ab98310f-75f7-45d1-9b99-d52cfef3fec3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Canon critique", "children": [{"id": "7fcb2ea5-2432-4b59-8a2a-6184de977f94", "type": "concept", "title": "anthologies"}, {"id": "90bd5be5-b21f-4bb0-8e65-4ec0d4f0e0c1", "type": "concept", "title": "syllabi"}, {"id": "16162d84-112c-4e25-b6b7-dfdafd56e1ef", "type": "concept", "title": "reviews"}, {"id": "e99f29c1-a064-4d23-9a60-e6639b755780", "type": "concept", "title": "libraries"}, {"id": "987e2534-3121-4c72-9ce3-6004b90e8111", "type": "concept", "title": "archive politics"}, {"id": "9438780d-20ce-4b2e-a63a-d08dd541a166", "type": "concept", "title": "tokenism"}, {"id": "2a703f27-e751-4139-a632-1107be907628", "type": "concept", "title": "recovery work"}, {"id": "536da733-769f-4528-9d28-ea0003edead1", "type": "concept", "title": "alternative reading lists"}], "description": "Students learn to ask why some writers become central while others remain marginal."}]}, {"id": "312aff5b-dd72-4699-9467-252b9c3f390f", "type": "topic", "t